==In animation==
[[File:Johto Route 34 Day Care anime.png|thumb|250px|Route 34 Day Care in {{aniseries|GS}}]]
===''Pokémon the Series''===
===={{aniseries|GS}}====
Route 34 appeared from ''[[EP146|Tricks of the Trade]]'' to ''[[EP157|The Fortune Hunters]]'', although some of the intervening episodes, such as ''[[EP154|Fowl Play!]]'', may have taken place in [[Ilex Forest]] instead. The route's landmarks include [[Palmpona]], [[Len Town]], [[Olesia]]'s {{p|Wooper}} preschool, and [[Onix Tunnel]]. {{Ash}} {{pkmn2|caught}} his {{AP|Totodile}} around this area in ''[[EP151|The Totodile Duel]]''. In ''The Fortune Hunters'', {{ashfr|Ash's group}} visited a {{pkmn|Day Care}} located in this area, similar to the {{pkmn|games}}, although this particular Day Care turned out to be just a front for [[Butch]] and [[Cassidy]]'s latest Pokémon-stealing scheme.
{{-}}

==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
[[File:Johto Route 34 Adventures.png|thumb|230px|Route 34 in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
===={{MangaArc|Gold, Silver & Crystal}}====
Route 34 first appeared in ''[[PS107|Gligar Glide]]'', where {{adv|Gold}} was spending a night there, when the {{pkmn|Egg}} that [[Professor Elm]] had entrusted with him hatched into a [[Togebo|Togepi]] while he slept. While Professor Elm was happy to learn that Gold had succeeded in hatching the Egg, he was outraged when it turned out Gold had inadvertently caused Togepi to pick up his gambling habits before the {{pkmn|category|Spike Ball Pokémon}} had even hatched. The {{pkmn|Professor}} then sent Gold to check out the [[Pokémon Day Care]], from where Togepi's Egg had been found. After Gold had helped the [[Day-Care Couple]] catch some runaway [[baby Pokémon]], the Day-Care Lady invited him for some {{pkmn|training}} inside the Day Care. Meanwhile, the Day-Care Man made a phone call to [[Jasmine]], revealing that Gold's Togepi was actually the offspring of her two {{p|Togetic}}, and inviting her to come take a look at it.

In ''[[PS108|Quilava Quandary]]'', the Day-Care Lady locked Gold into a room filled with powerful Pokémon and told him to battle them for his training. While reluctant at first, Gold was quickly forced to battle the Pokémon, although the Day-Care Lady forced him to do so without the goggles and {{wp|cue stick}} he usually used. While Gold was undergoing his training, the Day-Care Lady mused to herself how she was taking advantage of Gold's desire to train in order to make him make some of their lethargic Pokémon get some exercise without her having to do anything. As a result of the training, Gold's {{p|Cyndaquil}}, [[Exbo]], ended up [[Evolution|evolving]] into {{p|Quilava}}. When the Day-Care Couple heard of an earthquake that had struck [[Ecruteak City]], they got worried of Jasmine's safety and told Gold to go find her, giving him a [[King's Rock]] as a reward for completing his training.

In ''[[PS159|Popular Pupitar]]'', {{adv|Yellow}} found herself and her uncle [[Wilton]] at the Day Care after {{DL|Tower duo (Adventures)|Lugia}} had attacked their boat at the [[Whirl Islands]]. In ''[[PS160|Playful Porygon2]]'', the Day-Care Couple revealed that the medics who had saved them had brought them to the Day Care, based on a sketch of Jasmine in Yellow's notebook. In addition, Yellow and {{adv|Red}}'s {{p|Pikachu}}, [[Chuchu]] and [[Pika]], had gotten friendly with each other while Yellow was unconscious and had ended up producing an Egg together, much to Yellow's shock.

In ''[[PS173|The Last Battle VII]]'', the Day Care was attacked by [[Neo Team Rocket]] {{tc|Team Rocket Grunt|Grunts}}, who tried to steal the [[Rainbow Feather|Rainbow]] and [[Silver Feather|Silver Wings]] that {{adv|Green}} had hidden on Yellow's straw hat. Fortunately, though, Yellow managed to escape from them and fled to [[Ilex Forest]].

==Trivia==
* In {{game|HeartGold and SoulSilver|s}}, there is a [[List of glitches in Generation IV#Ace Trainer Kate oversight|glitch]] with {{tc|Ace Trainer}} Kate. She will only battle the player if they walk straight down the path. If the player walks to either side of her, she will apologize as she would after the player has defeated her. If the player walks down the path towards her after talking to her on the side she will somehow see them while facing the wrong way and then battle.
* In the Japanese versions, the three {{tc|Ace Trainer}} sisters all have names which start with "Mari".
* The Day Care man has [https://github.com/iimarckus/iimarck.us/blob/master/dumps/dcrystal.txt#L39945 an unused piece of dialogue] in the [[Generation II]] games, ''"Not yet..."''. This would likely be used during the breeding process to notify the player that the game needs more time to generate the {{pkmn|Egg}}.

